      ],
      "source_char_length": 20847,
      "evidence_catalog": {
        "e1": {
          "case_id": "011904",
          "source_hash": "c2bc7c0944a5ee103368055f7d2f0e3c260d4bb8336d406c3d01733304c96b12",
          "start_char": 5394,
          "end_char": 5680,
          "quote": "[10]\r\nIn a recent decision, Madam Justice Eleanor Dawson, examined the standard of review applicable to findings regarding state protection and concluded that in light of <FRAGMENT_SUPPRESSED> , above, the standard remains that of reasonableness (\r\n <FRAGMENT_SUPPRESSED>  at para. 6). "
        },
        "e2": {
          "case_id": "011904",
          "source_hash": "c2bc7c0944a5ee103368055f7d2f0e3c260d4bb8336d406c3d01733304c96b12",
          "start_char": 5680,
          "end_char": 5910,
          "quote": "Thus, pursuant to the reasonableness standard, the analysis of the Board's decision will be concerned with \"the existence of justification, transparency and intelligibility within the decision-making process [and also with] [...] "
        },
        "e3": {
          "case_id": "011904",
          "source_hash": "c2bc7c0944a5ee103368055f7d2f0e3c260d4bb8336d406c3d01733304c96b12",
          "start_char": 5910,
          "end_char": 6087,
          "quote": "whether the decision falls within a range of possible, acceptable outcomes which are defensible in respect of the facts and law\" ( <FRAGMENT_SUPPRESSED> , above, at para. 47).\r\n"
        },
        "e4": {
          "case_id": "011904",
          "source_hash": "c2bc7c0944a5ee103368055f7d2f0e3c260d4bb8336d406c3d01733304c96b12",
          "start_char": 6763,
          "end_char": 7028,
          "quote": "[13]\r\nIt is true that \"clear and convincing confirmation\" of a state's inability to protect must be put forth by an applicant, and that absent such proof, it is to be presumed that a state can protect its own citizens (\r\n <FRAGMENT_SUPPRESSED>  (QL), at para. 50). "
        },
        "e5": {
          "case_id": "011904",
          "source_hash": "c2bc7c0944a5ee103368055f7d2f0e3c260d4bb8336d406c3d01733304c96b12",
          "start_char": 7028,
          "end_char": 7276,
          "quote": "In this context, the more democratic a state is, the more the individual must have done to exhaust all avenues of protection available (\r\n <FRAGMENT_SUPPRESSED>  (QL), at para. 5;\r\n <FRAGMENT_SUPPRESSED>  [2007] F.C.J. No. 584 (QL), at para. 57).\r\n"
        },
        "e6": {
          "case_id": "011904",
          "source_hash": "c2bc7c0944a5ee103368055f7d2f0e3c260d4bb8336d406c3d01733304c96b12",
          "start_char": 7276,
          "end_char": 7618,
          "quote": "[14]\r\nIn the recent decision of <FRAGMENT_SUPPRESSED> , above, at para. 54 the Federal Court of Appeal noted that \"[t] he presumption of state protection described in\r\nWard\r\n, therefore, applies equally to cases where an individual claims to fear persecution by non-state entities and to cases where the state is alleged to be a persecutor.\" "
        },
        "e7": {
          "case_id": "011904",
          "source_hash": "c2bc7c0944a5ee103368055f7d2f0e3c260d4bb8336d406c3d01733304c96b12",
          "start_char": 7618,
          "end_char": 7773,
          "quote": "Thus, the existence of state persecuting agents does not serve to automatically rebut the presumption that a state is capable of protecting its citizens.\r\n"
        },
        "e8": {
          "case_id": "011904",
          "source_hash": "c2bc7c0944a5ee103368055f7d2f0e3c260d4bb8336d406c3d01733304c96b12",
          "start_char": 8352,
          "end_char": 8589,
          "quote": "[16]\r\nWhile the burden placed on claimants from developed democratic states is a high one, I remain of the view that this burden does not require that they put themselves in danger in order to exhaust all possible avenues of protection. "
        },
        "e9": {
          "case_id": "011904",
          "source_hash": "c2bc7c0944a5ee103368055f7d2f0e3c260d4bb8336d406c3d01733304c96b12",
          "start_char": 8589,
          "end_char": 8772,
          "quote": "Indeed, as Justice LaForest indicated, an individual will be required to seek state protection where it would be objectively unreasonable not to do so (\r\nWard\r\n, above, at para. 49). "
        },
        "e10": {
          "case_id": "011904",
          "source_hash": "c2bc7c0944a5ee103368055f7d2f0e3c260d4bb8336d406c3d01733304c96b12",
          "start_char": 8772,
          "end_char": 8841,
          "quote": "In <FRAGMENT_SUPPRESSED> , above, at para. 18, I stated that:\r\n[...] "
        },
        "e11": {
          "case_id": "011904",
          "source_hash": "c2bc7c0944a5ee103368055f7d2f0e3c260d4bb8336d406c3d01733304c96b12",
          "start_char": 8841,
          "end_char": 9116,
          "quote": "notwithstanding that not every member of the [police] was implicated in the applicant's persecution, seeking help from the [police], - asking, in effect, the [police] to protect the applicant from itself - would have in all likelihood placed the applicant in greater peril.\r\n"
        },
        "e12": {
          "case_id": "011904",
          "source_hash": "c2bc7c0944a5ee103368055f7d2f0e3c260d4bb8336d406c3d01733304c96b12",
          "start_char": 9116,
          "end_char": 9333,
          "quote": "Indeed, in my opinion, the requirement of having to place oneself in danger in order to exhaust all protection avenues would constitute an \"exceptional circumstance\" referred to by the Federal Court of Appeal above.\r\n"
        },
        "e13": {
          "case_id": "011904",
          "source_hash": "c2bc7c0944a5ee103368055f7d2f0e3c260d4bb8336d406c3d01733304c96b12",
          "start_char": 11681,
          "end_char": 11795,
          "quote": "[20]\r\nI find Madam Justice Gauthier's approach to the presumption of state protection in Mexico to be persuasive. "
        },
        "e14": {
          "case_id": "011904",
          "source_hash": "c2bc7c0944a5ee103368055f7d2f0e3c260d4bb8336d406c3d01733304c96b12",
          "start_char": 11795,
          "end_char": 11930,
          "quote": "While Mexico is a democracy and generally willing to protect its citizens, its governance and corruption problems are well documented. "
        },
        "e15": {
          "case_id": "011904",
          "source_hash": "c2bc7c0944a5ee103368055f7d2f0e3c260d4bb8336d406c3d01733304c96b12",
          "start_char": 11930,
          "end_char": 12101,
          "quote": "Accordingly, decision-makers must engage in a full assessment of the evidence placed before them suggesting that Mexico, while willing to protect, may be unable to do so. "
        },
        "e16": {
          "case_id": "011904",
          "source_hash": "c2bc7c0944a5ee103368055f7d2f0e3c260d4bb8336d406c3d01733304c96b12",
          "start_char": 12101,
          "end_char": 12414,
          "quote": "This assessment should include the context of the country of origin in general, all the steps that the applicants did in fact take, and their interaction with the authorities (\r\n <FRAGMENT_SUPPRESSED>  [2007] F.C.J. No. 1563 (QL), at para. 21;\r\n <FRAGMENT_SUPPRESSED>  [2002] F.C.J. No. 1331 (QL), at para. 18).\r\n"
        },
        "e17": {
          "case_id": "011904",
          "source_hash": "c2bc7c0944a5ee103368055f7d2f0e3c260d4bb8336d406c3d01733304c96b12",
          "start_char": 13761,
          "end_char": 14076,
          "quote": "[25]\r\nI am of the view that these alternate institutions do not constitute avenues of protection\r\nper se\r\n; unless there is evidence to the contrary, the police force is the only institution mandated with the protection of a nation's citizens and in possession of enforcement powers commensurate with this mandate. "
        },
        "e18": {
          "case_id": "011904",
          "source_hash": "c2bc7c0944a5ee103368055f7d2f0e3c260d4bb8336d406c3d01733304c96b12",
          "start_char": 14076,
          "end_char": 14352,
          "quote": "For example, the documentary evidence explicitly states that the National Human Rights Commission has no legal power of enforcement (\"Mexico: Situation of Witness to Crime and Corruption, Women Victims of Violence and Victims of Discrimination Based on Sexual Orientation\").\r\n"
        },
        "e19": {
          "case_id": "011904",
          "source_hash": "c2bc7c0944a5ee103368055f7d2f0e3c260d4bb8336d406c3d01733304c96b12",
          "start_char": 14352,
          "end_char": 14467,
          "quote": "[26]\r\nThe Board's decision points to many efforts being made by the state to protect women from domestic violence. "
        },
        "e20": {
          "case_id": "011904",
          "source_hash": "c2bc7c0944a5ee103368055f7d2f0e3c260d4bb8336d406c3d01733304c96b12",
          "start_char": 14467,
          "end_char": 14828,
          "quote": "However, what was important was for the Board to be satisfied that the protection offered in Mexico was effective (\r\n <FRAGMENT_SUPPRESSED>  [2007] F.C.J. No. 1733 (QL), at para. 16;\r\n <FRAGMENT_SUPPRESSED>  [2007] F.C.J. No. 118 (QL), at para. 15;\r\n <FRAGMENT_SUPPRESSED>  [2006] F.C.J. No. 439 (QL), at para. 34;\r\n <FRAGMENT_SUPPRESSED>  (QL), at para. 15).\r\n"
        },
        "e21": {
          "case_id": "011904",
          "source_hash": "c2bc7c0944a5ee103368055f7d2f0e3c260d4bb8336d406c3d01733304c96b12",
          "start_char": 15205,
          "end_char": 15570,
          "quote": "[28]\r\nThis Court has consistently held that where there is contradictory evidence before the Board, it must provide reasons why it did not consider this evidence relevant or trustworthy (\r\n <FRAGMENT_SUPPRESSED>  [2006] F.C.J. No. 1224 (QL), at para. 44;\r\n <FRAGMENT_SUPPRESSED>  [2004] F.C.J. No. 43 (QL), at para. 9;\r\n <FRAGMENT_SUPPRESSED>  (QL), at para. 15).\r\n"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "case_id": "045155",
      "source_hash": "93d2b91c8a6c01ef4c8d7fd08543035b0d0a400e103c668c828407f99ee2d6eb",
      "scopes": [
